rface | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Fenced `- Profile:` | Held (G33h + `_uncoded_lines`) |\n| Inline-code whole-line | Held (no `- profile:` prefix match) |\n| Full-width colon Profile | Treated absent → skip / hard gate when activated |\n| **Fenced evidence-index table** | **Broken** — `_parse_markdown_table` ignores fences |\n\n**Attack F1 — false-positive anomaly**\n\nLive evidence has `health=missing`, but a **fenced** all-`valid` table appears first:\n\n| Expected | Actual (a69ae03 blob) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `loop_autocontinue_anomaly=0` | **`anomaly=1`**, `skipped_unparsable=0` |\n\n**Attack F1b — silent false-negative**\n\nFenced `missing` first, live all-`valid` second:\n\n| Expected | Actual |\n| --- | --- |\n| `anomaly=1` or at least `skipped>0` | **`anomaly=0`, `skipped=0`** |\n\n### 2. Silent zero-check — FAIL (partial)\n\n- Unparsable preconditions → `skipped_unparsable` (visible, intentional).\n- F1b fenced determinate False → **silent ordinary non-trigger**.\n- Empty `- Profile:` when activated → **no** `loop-contract-profile-missing` (`raw=''` not `None`); only `skipped=1`.\n\n### 3. Regex / `int()` Unicode — FAIL\n\n`_latest_round_decision_text` uses `int(round_dir.name)`; `int(\"００１０\")==10`.\n\n**Attack I1**: `0009` Feedback=positive + decoy `００１０` Feedback=negative → **`anomaly=0, skipped=0`**; without decoy → `anomaly=1`.\n\n### 4. Cross-time-layer joins — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nLatest-only evaluation deliberate (G33i); activation-by-any-historical-Predecessor intentional for B.1. No new retroactive per-round hard red beyond already-registered families.\n\n### 5. Teeth quality — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nG33a–i are real paired mutations. Missing teeth for F1/F1b, I1, empty Profile under activation.\n\n### 6. OUT honesty — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nUpper bounds (partial preconditions, polarity-as-switch, prose-only ack, file-vs-field split) are well documented. **Under-disclosed**: evidence first-table-wins without fence stripping can invert the evidence condition; IN text implies the live table.\n\nCanonical fields correctly defeat Chinese「不需要」substring false positives on free-text rows.\n\n## Decisions / deviations\n\nReviewed exact `a69ae03` tree via `git show` + isolated import. F-01 elevated to P0 because false positives are the failure mode the commit’s own rationale calls mechanism-killing. F-01/F-02 still present on current HEAD for these call sites (noted, not credited).\n\n## Open questions\n\nnone\n\n## Verdict\n\n**FAIL**\n\n## Next recommendation\n\n1. Strip fenced blocks (or ignore fenced tables) before evidence-index parse; never prefer a fenced example over the live table.\n2. Choose latest round with ASCII-only names (`[0-9]{4}` / strict RE), never bare `int(name)`.\n3. Treat empty/non-enum `Profile:` when activated as hard `loop-contract-profile-missing` (or sibling).\n4. Add G33 paired teeth for F1, F1b, I1, empty Profile.\n5. Do not promote anomaly to a hard gate until F-01 polarity is closed.",
